@QRHub_HostAddress = http://localhost:5143

### 1. Register a New User
# @name register
POST {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2. Login to get JWT Token
# @name login
POST {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store the token from login response
@authToken = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

### 3. Get Authenticated User Profile
GET {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Create a Customized QR Code (High Error Correction, Custom Colors)
# @name createQr
POST {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My Portfolio Website",
  "content": "https://krishnagupta.dev",
  "description": "Personal developer portfolio and projects showcase",
  "foregroundColorHex": "#0A66C2",
  "backgroundColorHex": "#F3F4F6",
  "errorCorrectionLevel": "H",
  "pixelsPerModule": 20
}

### Store created QR code ID
@qrCodeId = {{createQr.response.body.data.id}}

### 5. Create a Second QR Code (WiFi access)
POST {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Office Guest WiFi",
  "content": "WIFI:S:CompanyGuest;T:WPA;P:Welcome2026!;;",
  "description": "Guest lounge WiFi network",
  "foregroundColorHex": "#111827",
  "backgroundColorHex": "#FFFFFF",
  "errorCorrectionLevel": "M",
  "pixelsPerModule": 15
}

### 6. Get All QR Codes for Current User (Paginated)
GET {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10&sortBy=CreatedAtUtc&sortDescending=true
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 7. Search QR Codes by Title / Content
GET {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes?searchTerm=WiFi
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Get QR Code Details by ID
GET {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes/{{qrCodeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Download or View Raw QR Code Image (PNG)
GET {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes/{{qrCodeId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 10. Update QR Code Details and Colors
PUT {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes/{{qrCodeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Portfolio Website",
  "content": "https://krishnagupta.dev/projects",
  "description": "Updated direct link to projects showcase",
  "foregroundColorHex": "#059669",
  "backgroundColorHex": "#ECFDF5",
  "errorCorrectionLevel": "Q",
  "pixelsPerModule": 22
}

### 11. Quick Generate QR Code Image via GET (Public, No Auth Needed)
GET {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes/quick-generate?content=https://github.com&foregroundColor=%237C3AED&backgroundColor=%23F5F3FF&pixelsPerModule=20

### 12. Quick Generate QR Code via POST (Public, No Auth Needed)
POST {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes/quick-generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "https://dotnet.microsoft.com",
  "foregroundColorHex": "#512BD4",
  "backgroundColorHex": "#FFFFFF",
  "errorCorrectionLevel": "H",
  "pixelsPerModule": 20
}

### 13. Delete a QR Code by ID
DELETE {{QRHub_HostAddress}}/api/qrcodes/{{qrCodeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json
